BEGIN:VEVENT
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
DESCRIPTION:Each year candidates from around the world are selected for th
 e Rhodes Scholarship to support a minimum of two years of graduate study 
 in any field at the University of Oxford. Rhodes Scholars are chosen not 
 only for their outstanding scholarly achievements\, but for their charact
 er\, commitment to others and to the common good\, and for their potentia
 l for leadership in whatever domains their careers may lead. \nCandidates
  who are not U.S. citizens\, permanent residents\, or DACA recipients may
  be eligible to apply in certain Rhodes constituencies. Prospective candi
 dates should review Davidson's Non-U.S. Rhodes Scholarship Application To
 olkit (Davidson login through your browser required to access) for inform
 ation.\n \nProgram Information: Check your constituency eligibility on th
 e Rhodes Trust website and Davidson's toolkitApplication Deadline: Varies
  by constituencyGeneral Eligibility: Varies by constituency\n*Candidates 
 who are U.S. citizens\, permanent residents\, or DACA recipients must app
 ly in the U.S. Rhodes constituency and must be endorsed by Davidson Colle
 ge. U.S. candidates should visit fellowships.davidson.edu/Rhodes and foll
 ow the link to the U.S. Rhodes application toolkit for details (Davidson 
 login through your browser required to access).\n\nHosted by: Catalyst\, 
 International Student Engagement\, Office of Fellowships\n\nOnline Locati
 on: https://fellowships.davidson.edu/NonUSRhodes\n\nAdditional Informatio
 n can be found at: https://wildcatsync.davidson.edu/event/12490505
DTEND:20261001T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260930T143828Z
DTSTART:20260723T160000Z
LOCATION:Online
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rhodes Scholarship (Non-U.S. Constituency) Application Deadlines: 
 Vary throughout summer/autumn 2026
UID:https://wildcatsync.davidson.edu/event/12490505
URL:https://wildcatsync.davidson.edu/event/12490505
X-HOSTS:Office of Fellowships
END:VEVENT
